<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">10 events that happened on 1 February, from 1327 to 2003.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1327">1327 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">699 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward III crowned after his father's deposition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fourteen-year-old Edward III was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a> after Queen Isabella and Roger Mortimer forced Edward II from the throne. His later claim to the French crown began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1790">1790 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">236 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Supreme Court gathers for its first session</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Supreme Court convened at the Merchants' Exchange in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, though too few justices had arrived to begin business until the next day. It heard no cases in its first year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/france" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Revolutionary France declares war on Britain and the Dutch Republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after executing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. The conflict that followed lasted, with brief pauses, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> in 1815.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1861">1861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texas votes to secede from the Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> convention voted 166 to 8 for secession, a decision confirmed by referendum later that month. Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Sam Houston</a> refused to swear loyalty to the Confederacy and was removed from office.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln signs the resolution for the Thirteenth Amendment</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> added his signature to the congressional resolution sending the amendment to abolish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> to the states, though presidents play no formal role in amendments. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> ratified it that day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Puccini's 'La bohème' premieres in Turin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Conducted by the young Arturo Toscanini at the Teatro Regio, Puccini's opera of struggling artists in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> received a cool critical welcome. Audiences loved it, and it became one of the most performed operas.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royal Canadian Mounted Police is formed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Royal North-West Mounted Police merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> Police to form the RCMP, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s national police force. Its scarlet tunics became one of the country's best-known symbols.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1946">1946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Trygve Lie becomes the first UN Secretary-General</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The General Assembly appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>'s foreign minister Trygve Lie as the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secretary-general-of-the-united-nations">Secretary-General of the United Nations</a>. He served until 1952, resigning after Soviet opposition over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Greensboro sit-in begins at a Woolworth's lunch counter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four Black students sat at a whites-only lunch counter in Greensboro, North Carolina, and stayed after being refused service. Sit-ins spread across the South, and Woolworth's desegregated the counter that July.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2003">2003 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">23 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Space Shuttle Columbia breaks up on re-entry</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Columbia disintegrated over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> minutes before landing, killing all seven astronauts. Hot gases had entered a wing damaged by foam at launch; shuttle flights were suspended for two and a half years.</p></div></li></ol>
